  "notes": "{買|か}い{取|と}る means to purchase something outright, often used for secondhand goods, trade-ins, and buybacks.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: 〜を{買|か}い{取|と}る\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {高|たか}く{買|か}い{取|と}る: to buy at a high price\n- {安|やす}く{買|か}い{取|と}る: to buy at a low price\n- {買|か}い{取|と}ってもらう: to have someone buy (from you)\n- {買|か}い{取|と}り{専門店|せんもんてん}: specialty buyback shop\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {買取|かいとり}: purchase, buyback (noun form)\n- {買取|かいとり}{価格|かかく}: buyback price\n- {下取|したど}り: trade-in\n\nUSAGE:\nVery common in the context of secondhand shops (リサイクルショップ), used bookstores ({古本屋|ふるほんや}), and electronics resellers. Signs reading {高価|こうか}{買取|かいとり} (we buy at high prices) are common.",
